  "question": {
    "text": "An octahedral complex with molecular composition M.5NH<sub>3</sub>.Cl.SO<sub>4</sub> has two isomers, A and B. The solution of A gives a white precipitate with AgNO<sub>3</sub> solution and the solution of B gives white precipitate with BaCl<sub>2</sub> solution .The type of isomerism exhibited by the complex is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eM3Hu",
      "text": "Coordinate isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WiMq1",
      "text": "Geometrical isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mtAAx",
      "text": "Ionisation isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PlXKi",
      "text": "Linkage isomerism",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The central metal atom M is in +3 oxidation state and ionisation isomers due to exchange of ligands outside&nbsp; &amp; inside the co-ordination sphere are<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></munder><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mover><munder><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&#8595;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <munder> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>M</mi><msub> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><msub> <mi>H</mi> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo> </mrow> <mn>5</mn> </msub> <mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo> </mrow> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo> </mrow> </munder> <mi>S</mi><msub> <mi>O</mi> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <mover> <mo>&#8594;</mo> <mrow> <mi>B</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>C</mi><msub> <mi>l</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mover> <munder> <mrow> <mi>B</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>S</mi><msub> <mi>O</mi> <mn>4</mn> </msub> <msub> <mrow></mrow> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo> </mrow> </msub> <mo>&#8595;</mo> </mrow> <mrow> <mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi> </mrow> </munder> </mrow> </math><br /><br />[A] and [B] are ionisation isomers</p></blockquote>",
